## Why This Is Asked

Safety-critical navigation in urban environments requires reliable 3D pose estimation and intent understanding from monocular video. A new angle tests on-device adaptation to unseen clothing and backpacks, plus robust temporal reasoning under occlusion, aligning with real-world edge deployments.

## Key Concepts

- Monocular 3D pose estimation from a single RGB stream
- Pedestrian intent recognition for near-term collisions
- Edge latency constraints and adapter-based on-device learning
- Synthetic+real data strategies to cover diverse outfits and behaviors
- Temporal consistency and occlusion robustness in losses

## Code Example

```javascript
function computeLoss(outputs, targets) {
  const poseLoss = l2(outputs.pose, targets.pose);
  const intentLoss = crossEntropy(outputs.intent, targets.intent);
  const temporalLoss = smoothL1(outputs.posePrev, outputs.pose);
  return poseLoss + 0.5 * intentLoss + 0.2 * temporalLoss;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you evaluate 3D pose accuracy and intent classification in crowded urban scenes?
- What mechanisms ensure adapters do not drift over successive 5-shot updates?

## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates robust multi-hand 3D pose with fine-grained articulation under occlusion, plus on-device adaptation for real-world diversity.

## Key Concepts
- 3D hand pose (finger joints), hand mesh (MANO)
- Temporal tracking and occlusion handling
- On-device few-shot adaptation and edge latency

## Code Example
```javascript
function totalLoss(key3d, pred3d, mesh3d, predMesh3d, tio, contactPred, contactGT){
  const lKey = mse(key3d, pred3d);
  const lMesh = l2(mesh3d, predMesh3d);
  const lTemp = mse(pred3d, tio);
  const lContact = crossEntropy(contactGT, contactPred);
  return 0.4*lKey + 0.3*lMesh + 0.2*lTemp + 0.1*lContact;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you evaluate hand-object contact reliability in clutter?
- What ablations would you run to isolate the impact of articulation accuracy vs. contact estimation?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses on-device CV design, latency budgeting, and robust 3D human pose estimation for safety-critical driving.

## Key Concepts
- On-device real-time inference with a lightweight backbone
- 2D-to-3D pose reconstruction and Kalman filtering
- Self-supervised pretraining from unlabeled video
- Robustness to occlusion and adverse weather
- Quantization and latency accounting

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode for pipeline
class PedestrianPoseEstimator {
  constructor() { /* load detector, 3D head, PnP module, tracker */ }
  forward(frame) {
    const keypoints2D = this.detector.detect(frame)
    const pose3D = this.poseHead.estimate(keypoints2D)
    const pose6DoF = differentiablePnP(pose3D, this.cameraIntrinsics)
    return this.tracker.update(pose6DoF)
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you extend this to multi-pedestrian tracking with identity preservation?
- What failure modes are most critical in heavy rain and how would you mitigate them?
